  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This tetra is only very rarely available. The large species can attain a maximum length of about 60 cm and 7 kg of weight.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Moonfish, Citharinus citharus, was imported from Nigeria. In its home countries, the moonfish is a much esteemed food fish. But the species is also very interesting in respect of aquarium keeping.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>It makes an interesting inhabitant for very large aquaria. Suitable for very large aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Most worth mentioning is the mouth structure, which is very similar to that of the night tetras (Semaprochilodus) from South America and the Kissing Gouramis (Helostoma) from Southeast Asia. Like these, the Moonfish feeds mainly on Aufwuchs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Against conspecifics and also against other fish the Moonfish is quite peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/citharinus_citharus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The calm silver discs are very interesting.</p>"
    }
  ],
